      "text": "Given that 7 identical bowling balls weigh the same as 3 identical canoes, we start by letting \\( B \\) represent the weight of one bowling ball and \\( C \\) represent the weight of one canoe. According to the problem, we can write the equation:\n\n\\[\n7B = 3C\n\\]\n\nWe are also given that the total weight of two canoes is 56 pounds. Therefore, we can express this relationship as:\n\n\\[\n2C = 56\n\\]\n\nTo find the weight of one canoe, we solve for \\( C \\):\n\n\\[\nC = \\frac{56}{2} = 28 \\text{ pounds}\n\\]\n\nNext, we substitute \\( C = 28 \\) back into the equation \\( 7B = 3C \\):\n\n\\[\n7B = 3 \\times 28\n\\]\n\nSimplify the right-hand side:\n\n\\[\n7B = 84\n\\]\n\nTo find \\( B \\), we divide both sides by 7:\n\n\\[\nB = \\frac{84}{7} = 12 \\text{ pounds}\n\\]\n\nThus, the weight of one bowling ball is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{12}\n\\]",
